-- title:
--   The integer bound `L₁ L₂ ≤ (ℓ + q + 7)(4q + 12)` (`log_nat`)
-- statement:
--   The integer bound `L₁ L₂ ≤ (ℓ + q + 7)(4q + 12)`.
--
--   The following holds (Lean statement, in the scope of module `Solutions.KFMLog18a`):
--
--   ```lean
--   theorem NLogN.KFV.P18M.log_nat (P ℓ q : ℕ) (hP7 : 7 ≤ P) (hℓP : ℓ ≤ P) (hq1 : 2 ^ q ≤ P) (hq2 : P < 2 ^ (q + 1)) :
--       (zsz ((2 * (kb P ℓ * 2 ^ ℓ + 2) + 1 : ℕ) : ℤ) + 2) *
--         (zsz (((zsz ((2 * (kb P ℓ * 2 ^ ℓ + 2) + 1 : ℕ) : ℤ) + 2) ^ 4 : ℕ) : ℤ) + 1) ≤
--         (ℓ + q + 7) * (4 * q + 12)
--   ```
--
--   **Context.** KFM Log18a: the logarithmic factor of the Kronecker products (`Log18Need`)
--
--   With `P = p = 6b` and `q = ⌊log₂ P⌋`: `kb < 2^{q+3}`, so `m + 1 < 2^{q+ℓ+5}` and
--   `L₁ = zsz(m+1) + 2 ≤ ℓ + q + 7 ≤ 3P`; then `L₁⁴ < 2^{4q+11}` and `L₂ ≤ 4q + 12`. Since
--   `q ≤ log₂ P` and `q ≤ ln P / ln 2 < 2 ln P`, `L₁ L₂ ≤ 84 (ℓ + log₂ P + 1)(ln P + 1)`.
--   Main result: **`log18Need : KFV.Log18Need`** (`c = 84`, no extra threshold).
